  "body": "## What changed\n\n- 3D Finish gets the shared field `pass_start` (`machining2d::PassStart`, #3316) in `OpParams::Finish3D`. There is no new type.\n- Project file: the shared key `pass_start` with the 3D Pocket serde attributes. Absent is Auto. `auto` is never written. There is no version step.\n- Digest: `digest::write_pass_start` writes the value only off Auto, and only for Contour and Flat. Every other op keeps its stamp.\n- Engine: new doors `finishing3d::contour_from(facets, p, start)` and `finishing3d::flat_from(facets, p, start)`. `contour` and `flat` keep their signatures and call the new doors with Auto. `Finish3DParams` does not change (the `direction_angle` pattern of #3426).\n- `shadow_pass` collects the runs of each offset pass. For Inside it reverses the sequence of the passes. Inside one pass the loop order does not change. No loop is added or removed. Project passes Auto.\n- `finishing3d::reads_pass_start(pattern)` is true only for Contour and Flat.\n- Page: the shared row `Pass starts at` on the 3D Finish Passes tab. For each other pattern a line under the row names the pattern: \"Not used with <pattern>: this pattern has no inside or outside ring order. Only Contour and Flat use it\".\n- MCP: the generic `edit_operation` (no kind-specific code).\n- Decision file: `docs/decisions/3362-pass-start-finish3d.md`.\n- Follow-up: #3624 \"Pass starts at: Geodesic start side\" (Geodesic shows the \"Not used\" line in this PR).\n\n## Hand trace of one level (Contour)\n\nFixture: a 20 x 20 x 10 mm block, a ball of radius 3, a stepover of 3 mm. The top face gives four offset passes. Each pass is one square loop. Half-widths from the block centre: P0 = 10, P1 = 7, P2 = 4, P3 = 1. T is the ring tail on the flanks (`rings_and_tail`).\n\n| Value | Cut order |\n|---|---|\n| Auto | P0, P1, P2, P3, T |\n| Outside | P0, P1, P2, P3, T (the same moves as Auto) |\n| Inside | P3, P2, P1, P0, T |\n\nEach run goes through the existing `emit_runs` link law: a vertical hop to retract or clearance; `diagonal_ok` when `ramp` is on; `straight_ok` when the gap link is Straight. The ring tail keeps its own laws. No new link type is used.\n\n## Readings\n\n- Inside and Auto have the same multiset of cutting moves (338 in Contour). The only move that differs is the rise out of the last loop before the ring tail. That rise starts at the end of the last loop, so it follows the order.\n- The verifier finds no blocking warning (`Warning::blocks_post`) for Auto, Inside and Outside, on Contour and on Flat (app test).\n- No sideways rapid at or below the top face for any value (motion test).\n- The seven Finish3D goldens in `golden_cl` do not move (`golden_cl` 33/33, no file in `crates/app/tests/golden/` changed).\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `crates/motion/tests/finish3d_pass_start.rs`:\n  - `inside_cuts_the_innermost_offset_pass_first_on_contour_and_flat`. It was red first, with the reverse disabled: `Contour: Inside cuts inside-out: [1000, 700, 400, 100, 1000]`.\n  - `auto_is_the_old_contour_and_flat_move_for_move`\n  - `only_the_nested_loop_patterns_read_pass_start`\n- `crates/app/tests/finish3d_pass_start.rs`:\n  - `the_generate_arm_hands_pass_start_to_contour_and_flat` (generate and verifier)\n  - `other_patterns_keep_their_paths_and_stamp_with_a_saved_pass_start`\n  - `finish3d_pass_start_rides_the_project_file`\n- `crates/app/tests/mcp/finish3d_pass_start.rs`: `finish3d_pass_start_uses_mcp_history_and_never_writes_auto` (in the `mcp` binary)\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/pass_start.rs`: `the_finish3d_passes_tab_offers_pass_start_and_names_the_unused_patterns`. The Finish3D Passes list in `tests.rs` now has \"Pass starts at\".\n\n## Gate (debug, by name, `-j 6`)\n\n- motion: `--no-run` for all test binaries OK. `--lib` 548 ok. `finish3d` 55 ok (33 ignored). `finish3d_gaplink` 7, `finish3d_holes` 5, `finish3d_land` 7, `finish3d_overhang_and_chord` 3, `scallop_ceiling` 4, `multiaxis` 7, `pocket3d_pass_start` 2, `pass_start_levels` 7, `finish3d_pass_start` 3. All pass.\n- app: `--lib` 299. `golden_cl` 33. `conformance` 7. `project_roundtrip` 80. `operations` 121. `mcp` 27. `mcp_doc_drift` 6. `finish3d_direction` 4. `area_controls` 13. `verify` 21. `shared_face_bodies_finish` 2. `docs_troubleshooting` 1. `example_catalog` 37, `example_catalog_adaptive` 1, `example_catalog_edge_work` 1. `first_part_programs` 2. `import_step_q02_mold` 1. `setup_align_3d` 6. `wcs_start` 6. `finish3d_pass_start` 3. All pass.\n- ui: `--lib` 1494 pass.\n- clippy `-D warnings`: motion `--all-targets`, ui `--all-targets`, app `--lib` and the changed app test binaries. All clean.\n\n## Not run\n\n- No heavy lane and no light lane (P2).\n- No app window. No pixel snapshot.\n- The `camcraft-mcp` skill text still names only 2D Offset for `pass_start`. It is a process file, so this PR does not change it.\n\nChangelog: 3D Finish: \"Pass starts at\" (Auto / Inside / Outside) on the Passes tab, in MCP and in the project file. Contour and Flat with Inside cut the innermost offset pass first. Auto keeps the earlier order. Other patterns say by name that they do not use it.\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nRefs #3316\nRefs #1448\n\nFixes #3362\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
